On iOS the launch screen and the splash after it are the launch mark on the
member theme's ground.

The package's launch screen fills the screen with a launch image on white,
and its splash view repeats it until the app is ready. Both now draw the
brand's `mark-primary.svg` centred at 96pt, three points a cell, so every
cell is whole pixels at 2x and 3x, on the ink theme's `canvas`. The mark and
the colour are named from the asset catalog, where the bridge's manifest
copies the brand's own SVG, kept as a vector, and the colour set
`scripts/brand_drawables.php` takes from the brand's tokens. The named
colour's value in the storyboard is what Interface Builder shows when the
catalog is not at hand; the catalog's colour is the one drawn.

